    "notes": "glob AbortSignal cancellation bypass (GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4), moderate. The advisory still lists >=9.0.0 <=14.0.1, but the fix was backported to 13.0.7 (dist-tag v13-legacy, 2026-11-06), which the lock now holds; the advisory range has not caught up, so 13.0.7 is still flagged. The remaining unpatched copy is 10.5.0 (legacy-v10, unchanged), reached only through babel-jest (directly and via jest) -> babel-plugin-istanbul -> test-exclude 7.x, which requires glob ^10.4.1. npm ls glob --omit=dev is empty, so nothing ships. Re-checked 2026-11-23. Three months, as for other dev-only waivers with no fix on a line: a re-check can only confirm the note, and a fix on another line may need a parent update rather than a lock change."
